---
import ComparePage from '../../../components/ComparePage.astro';

const compareRows = [
  { feature: 'AI-native (real LLMs)', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Autonomous AI Agents', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Contextual conversations', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Native appointments engine', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Official WhatsApp Business API', shadia: true, competitor: 'Partial' },
  { feature: 'Instagram + Facebook + TikTok', shadia: true, competitor: true },
  { feature: 'Proactive client reactivation', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Unified team workspace', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Spanish language support', shadia: true, competitor: false },
  { feature: 'Transparent SMB pricing', shadia: true, competitor: 'Partial' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: "What's the difference between Chatfuel and Shadia AI?", a: 'Chatfuel is a flow-based chatbot platform. Shadia AI has real AI agents that use LLMs to maintain contextual conversations, make decisions and operate autonomously. They are not the same type of product.' },
  { q: 'Can Chatfuel handle questions outside the predefined flow?', a: "Flow-based chatbots like Chatfuel can only respond to questions the bot creator anticipated. If a user asks an unexpected question, the bot fails or escalates to a human. Shadia's AI agents can handle open-ended conversations with real intelligence." },
];
---

<ComparePage
  lang="en"
  competitor="Chatfuel"
  competitorSlug="chatfuel"
  title="Shadia AI vs Chatfuel — Real AI Agents vs Flow Chatbots | Shadia AI"
  description="Compare Shadia AI vs Chatfuel. Autonomous AI agents with real LLMs vs predefined flow chatbots. The Chatfuel alternative for WhatsApp ."
  canonical="https://shadia.ai/en/compare/vs-chatfuel"
  ogImage="/og/compare-chatfuel-en.png"
  heroHeadline="Shadia AI vs Chatfuel — Real AI vs flow chatbot"
  heroSubheadline="Chatfuel builds chatbots that follow rules. Shadia AI has AI agents that think. The difference matters when your client asks a question nobody anticipated."
  verdictPoints={[
    'Shadia uses real LLMs for contextual conversations; Chatfuel uses predefined flows',
    "Shadia's agents handle any question; Chatfuel fails outside the flow",
    'Native appointments engine in Shadia; not available in Chatfuel',
    'Unified team workspace; Chatfuel has no team workspace for human agents',
    'Proactive client reactivation: exclusive to Shadia',
  ]}
  compareRows={compareRows}
  detailedText={`
    <h2>What does Chatfuel do well?</h2>
    <p>Chatfuel is good for creating simple FAQ chatbots and basic qualification flows on Facebook Messenger and Instagram. It's easy to set up for very simple use cases and doesn't require deep technical knowledge.</p>
    <h2>The fundamental limitation of Chatfuel</h2>
    <p>Chatfuel's limitation is inherent to its architecture: rule-based bots, not real artificial intelligence. When a client asks a question the bot creator didn't anticipate, the bot fails. In real sales or service conversations, this happens constantly.</p>
    <p>Shadia AI uses large language models (LLMs) to create agents that truly understand context, remember previous conversations and can handle unanticipated situations with real intelligence.</p>
    <h2>The practical difference</h2>
    <p>With Chatfuel, a client asks "do you have availability Tuesday at 3?" and the bot says "Sorry, I didn't understand. Please choose an option:" With Shadia, the agent checks real-time availability and responds: "Yes, Tuesday the 20th at 3 PM is available. Shall I confirm your appointment?"</p>
  `}
  migrationText="If you currently have flows in Chatfuel, we can convert them into real AI agents in Shadia. The onboarding process includes transferring all your business logic."
  faqs={faqs}
/>
